    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Regular waves in deep water",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The sea surface elevation is described by:",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "where",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/6ec5583e1d5da19d1479dd5657995cf0591dc3ccfabbe95850e13ec19e2a19a7.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/cdcd5d295a651c1c73e3523922c77ea245385034b2821296b644ab4f400ea5a5.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Wave frequency",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(rad/s)",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Phase velocity",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(m/sec)",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Wave length",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(m)",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Wave number",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(rad/m)",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "These expressions are only valid in deep water",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": ", where *h* is the water depth.",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Sailing condition",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The sailing condition of a vessel is given by its forward speed  *U*  and its encounter angle, i.e., the heading angle relative to the waves.",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Encounter angle",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Encounter frequency",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "If the waves are observed  from a reference frame that moves at a constant speed, the frequency observed is called Encounter Frequency.",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This is a Doppler effect",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Negative encounter frequency => vessel overtakes the waves",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 3
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ocean waves",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ocean waves present, in general, irregularity in time and space and cannot be predicted exactly: Stochastic Process.",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "ζ(x,y,0)",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "ζ(0,0,t)",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/a36cd32399347e00c35fb78ada8ab84582be682c65cd65ef23c71fc7b9c75ea2.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*t*",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 4
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Stochastic sea description",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In practice, it is assumed that the variations of a stochastic nature of the sea are much slower than the variations of the sea surface itself; Hence,",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- ζ(x, y, t) can be considered a realization of a stationary and homogeneous stochastic process.",
            "- For deep water waves, ζ(x, y, t) is further assumed Gaussian."
        ],
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 5
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Gaussian waves",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "p(ζ)",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "ζ(xo,yo,t)",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/a36cd32399347e00c35fb78ada8ab84582be682c65cd65ef23c71fc7b9c75ea2.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "*t*",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "ζ(x,y,0)",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "ζ",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(xo,yo)",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The elevation of the sea surface can be thought as being generated as the sum of many sinusoidal waves with different amplitudes, frequencies, and phases.",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 6
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "How good are these hypotheses?",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "From data collected at sea (Haverre & Moan, 1985), it can be stated that",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- For low and moderate seas (H1/3 < 4m), the sea can be considered stationary for periods over 20 min. For more severe sea states, stationarity can be questioned even for periods of 20 min.",
            "- For medium seas (4m < H1/3 < 8m), Gaussian models are still accurate, but deviations from Gaussianity slightly increase with the increasing severity of the sea state.",
            "- If the water is sufficiently deep, wave elevation can be consider Gaussian regardless of the sea state."
        ],
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(H1/3 is the average of the highest one third of the waves recorded.)",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 7
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Random sea characterization",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Under the Gaussianity assumption, the process is completely described by",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "list",
        "list_items": [
            "- Mean",
            "- Variance"
        ],
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The sea surface elevation is described relative to the mean free surface; therefore, the mean of the SP is zero.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The variance is described in terms of a sea power spectral density or sea spectrum.",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 8
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Power spectral density definition",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "If we use the frequency in Hz to define the FT, then",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\begin{array}{c}S_{xx}(f)=\\int_{}^{}R_{xx}(\\tau ) e^{-j2\\pi f\\tau }d\\tau \\\\R_{xx}(\\tau )=\\int_{}^{}S_{xx}(f) e^{j2\\pi f\\tau }df\\end{array}$",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "and",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$var\\left[x\\right]=R_{xx}(0)=\\int_{}^{}S_{xx}(f)df$",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "from which the name power spectral density follows.",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This definition is common in the literature of electrical communications and signal processing.",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "PSD alternative definition",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "When we use the circular frequency (rad/s) to define the FT,",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "$\\begin{array}{c}S_{xx}(\\omega )=a \\int_{}^{}R_{xx}(\\tau ) e^{-j\\omega \\tau }d\\tau \\\\R_{xx}(\\tau )=b \\int_{}^{}S_{xx}(\\omega ) e^{j\\omega \\tau }d\\omega \\\\a b=\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\end{array}$",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "We need to be careful on how we compute power!!!",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Random sea characterization",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The spectral moments of order *n* are defined as:",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "image",
        "img_path": "images/2db4e4696c528214baa5357da58a72bd806cdb22e3532c04e4a94efa732f6d63.jpg",
        "image_caption": [],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Then the variance and standard deviation (RMS value) are",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": " =",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Statistics of wave period",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One-day Tutorial, CAMS'07, Bol, Croatia",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "page_footnote",
        "text": "<number>",
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Narrow and wide banded processes",
        "text_level": 2,
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "06/06/26",
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
